1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,999
How does a company raise

2
00:00:01,999 --> 00:00:03,704
millions of dollars on the

3
00:00:03,704 --> 00:00:05,676
stock exchange, and what happens

4
00:00:05,676 --> 00:00:07,275
to the owners' stake when

5
00:00:07,275 --> 00:00:08,927
it does? Let's work through

6
00:00:08,927 --> 00:00:10,259
it with real numbers.

7
00:00:10,259 --> 00:00:12,178
This is Reian Creative Finance.

8
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:14,523
Understanding markets. Following capital.

9
00:00:14,873 --> 00:00:16,861
There are three main ways

10
00:00:16,861 --> 00:00:18,143
onto an exchange.

11
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:20,130
An initial public offering,

12
00:00:20,130 --> 00:00:21,990
or IPO, offers shares to

13
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:23,913
the public and can raise

14
00:00:23,913 --> 00:00:25,965
new money. News reports say

15
00:00:25,965 --> 00:00:28,593
Amalgamated Brands is raising about

16
00:00:28,593 --> 00:00:30,709
20 million dollars this way

17
00:00:30,709 --> 00:00:31,671
on the VFEX.

18
00:00:31,671 --> 00:00:34,107
A listing by introduction raises

19
00:00:34,107 --> 00:00:36,030
no money: shares that are

20
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:38,467
already widely held simply start

21
00:00:38,467 --> 00:00:40,583
trading. TSL was reported to

22
00:00:40,583 --> 00:00:42,314
move to the VFEX this

23
00:00:42,314 --> 00:00:43,275
way in 2026.

24
00:00:43,275 --> 00:00:45,519
And a private placement sells

25
00:00:45,519 --> 00:00:47,635
shares to selected investors.

26
00:00:47,985 --> 00:00:49,551
Now a crucial difference.

27
00:00:49,551 --> 00:00:51,225
When a company issues new

28
00:00:51,225 --> 00:00:52,791
shares, the cash goes to

29
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:54,789
the company, and existing owners

30
00:00:54,789 --> 00:00:56,355
are diluted. In an offer

31
00:00:56,355 --> 00:00:58,245
for sale, existing owners sell

32
00:00:58,245 --> 00:00:59,325
their own shares:

33
00:00:59,325 --> 00:01:00,782
the cash goes to them,

34
00:01:00,782 --> 00:01:02,402
and the number of shares

35
00:01:02,402 --> 00:01:04,184
doesn't change. Many IPOs mix

36
00:01:04,184 --> 00:01:06,290
both. Amalgamated Brands' offer was

37
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:08,180
reported to include 5 million

38
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,016
dollars of new shares within

39
00:01:10,016 --> 00:01:11,366
the 20 million total.

40
00:01:11,716 --> 00:01:13,404
Let's work an example with

41
00:01:13,404 --> 00:01:14,603
a made up company,

42
00:01:14,603 --> 00:01:15,692
Zim Agro Limited.

43
00:01:15,692 --> 00:01:17,326
It's valued at 15 million

44
00:01:17,326 --> 00:01:19,123
US dollars before the raise.

45
00:01:19,123 --> 00:01:21,029
That's the pre money valuation.

46
00:01:21,029 --> 00:01:22,663
It has 30 million shares,

47
00:01:22,663 --> 00:01:24,243
so each share is priced

48
00:01:24,243 --> 00:01:25,877
at 15 million divided by

49
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,401
30 million: 50 US cents.

50
00:01:27,401 --> 00:01:28,763
It wants to raise 5

51
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:30,615
million dollars of new money,

52
00:01:30,615 --> 00:01:32,140
so it issues 5 million

53
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:33,447
divided by 50 cents:

54
00:01:33,447 --> 00:01:34,863
10 million new shares.

55
00:01:35,213 --> 00:01:36,866
After the IPO there are

56
00:01:36,866 --> 00:01:38,064
40 million shares.

57
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:38,919
At 50 cents,

58
00:01:38,919 --> 00:01:40,572
the post money valuation,

59
00:01:40,572 --> 00:01:42,283
which is also the market

60
00:01:42,283 --> 00:01:44,678
capitalisation, is 20 million dollars.

61
00:01:44,678 --> 00:01:46,616
New investors own 10 million

62
00:01:46,616 --> 00:01:47,870
out of 40 million:

63
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:49,809
25 percent. The founders drop

64
00:01:49,809 --> 00:01:51,405
from 100 percent to 75

65
00:01:51,405 --> 00:01:52,888
percent. That's dilution.

66
00:01:52,888 --> 00:01:54,598
But their stake is still

67
00:01:54,598 --> 00:01:56,252
worth 15 million dollars,

68
00:01:56,252 --> 00:01:57,905
and the company now has

69
00:01:57,905 --> 00:01:59,730
5 million dollars of fresh

70
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:00,642
cash to grow.

71
00:02:00,992 --> 00:02:02,542
But wait. The ZSE main

72
00:02:02,542 --> 00:02:04,321
board wants 30 percent of

73
00:02:04,321 --> 00:02:05,871
shares in public hands,

74
00:02:05,871 --> 00:02:07,535
and our public only has

75
00:02:07,535 --> 00:02:08,856
25 percent. One fix:

76
00:02:08,856 --> 00:02:10,578
the founders also sell 2

77
00:02:10,578 --> 00:02:12,759
million of their existing shares

78
00:02:12,759 --> 00:02:14,251
in an offer for sale.

79
00:02:14,251 --> 00:02:16,203
That money, 1 million dollars,

80
00:02:16,203 --> 00:02:17,638
goes to the founders,

81
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:18,728
not the company.

82
00:02:18,728 --> 00:02:20,393
Now the public holds 12

83
00:02:20,393 --> 00:02:22,172
million out of 40 million:

84
00:02:22,172 --> 00:02:23,435
exactly 30 percent.

85
00:02:23,785 --> 00:02:25,587
The process runs like this.

86
00:02:25,587 --> 00:02:27,333
Advisers value the company,

87
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:28,572
using its earnings,

88
00:02:28,572 --> 00:02:30,712
its assets and comparable listed

89
00:02:30,712 --> 00:02:33,078
companies. The prospectus is prepared

90
00:02:33,078 --> 00:02:34,880
and approved, and the offer

91
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,288
opens. Investors apply,

92
00:02:36,288 --> 00:02:37,696
and if the offer is

93
00:02:37,696 --> 00:02:40,399
oversubscribed, allocations get scaled back.

94
00:02:40,399 --> 00:02:42,483
Finally the exchange grants the

95
00:02:42,483 --> 00:02:44,398
listing, and the shares start

96
00:02:44,398 --> 00:02:44,905
trading.

97
00:02:45,255 --> 00:02:46,800
And what happens to the

98
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,451
money? Companies use it to

99
00:02:48,451 --> 00:02:50,582
expand capacity, pay down expensive

100
00:02:50,582 --> 00:02:52,393
debt, or buy other businesses.

101
00:02:52,393 --> 00:02:53,351
As an investor,

102
00:02:53,351 --> 00:02:54,843
always read the use of

103
00:02:54,843 --> 00:02:56,973
proceeds section in the prospectus:

104
00:02:56,973 --> 00:02:58,625
it tells you whether your

105
00:02:58,625 --> 00:03:00,542
money is building the business,

106
00:03:00,542 --> 00:03:02,034
or just buying out the

107
00:03:02,034 --> 00:03:02,513
sellers.

108
00:03:02,863 --> 00:03:04,114
Dilution isn't loss:

109
00:03:04,114 --> 00:03:05,649
it can mean a smaller

110
00:03:05,649 --> 00:03:07,185
slice of a bigger pie.

111
00:03:07,185 --> 00:03:08,777
Know who gets the cash,

112
00:03:08,777 --> 00:03:10,597
and check the public float

113
00:03:10,597 --> 00:03:11,848
rule. In part four:

114
00:03:11,848 --> 00:03:13,099
life after listing.

